# Keep build output and local trees out of the context.
#
# Docker reads the leading `*` differently from git: its `*` is filepath.Match, which
# does not cross `/`, so it only excludes top-level entries. Once `!/src/` above
# re-includes src, NOTHING below it is excluded by default -- unlike .gitignore, where a
# slash-less `*` applies at every depth. The last matching pattern wins, so these
# exclusions must stay at the end of the file, after every `!/src/...` line.
#
# None of this ever reached the image (Dockerfile's only stage crossing is
# `COPY --from=app-build /workspace/deploy /app`); it only bloated the context.
/src/**/bin/
/src/**/obj/
# npm ci re-installs these in the app-build stage anyway.
/src/**/node_modules/
# Fable .jsx output; `dotnet run bundle` regenerates it (Build.fs `Clean`).
/src/**/output/
# Local scratch and the retired data tree (renamed data -> data_ by the AppPath
# refactor, f8f19359); untracked, nothing reads them.
/src/**/Scratch/
/src/**/data_/
